#. Tag: title
#: contrib.docbook:9
#, no-c-format
msgid "Contributing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I contribute to &kde;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; is a free software project that lives from voluntary contributions. "
"Everybody is encouraged to contribute to &kde;. Not only programmers are "
"welcome. There are many ways in which you can help to improve &kde;:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid "Test the software."
msgstr "Probar o software."

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Send in bug reports. For more information on this, see <link linkend=\"bug-"
"report\">How do I submit a bug report?</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:26
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Write documentation or help files. You can get some information by visiting "
"the <ulink url=\"http://l10n.kde.org/docs/\">&kde; Editorial Team Home Page</"
"ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Translate programs, documentation, and help files. For more information on "
"this, you should visit <ulink url=\"http://l10n.kde.org\">The &kde; "
"Translators' and Documenters' Web Site</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Draw nice icons or compose sound effects. You can visit the <ulink url="
"\"http://kde-artists.org/\">&kde; artists page</ulink> to find out more."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Write articles and books about &kde;. If you want to help spread the word "
"about &kde;, simply send an email to <email>kde-promo@kde.org</email>. This "
"will get you in touch with the &kde; public relations volunteers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Program new &kde; applications. Please refer to <xref linkend=\"programming"
"\"/> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid "Of course, sponsors are also welcome. :-)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are several places to look for more information if you want to get "
"involved in the development. The first step is to subscribe to some of the "
"<ulink url=\"http://www.kde.org/mailinglists/\">mailing lists</ulink>. You "
"will soon see something that can be improved or added."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I submit a bug report?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is a bug tracking system available at <ulink url=\"http://bugs.kde.org"
"\">http://bugs.kde.org</ulink>. The system features a wizard to submit new "
"bug reports and a list of all known bugs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The easiest way to submit a bug is to select <menuchoice><guimenu>Help</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Report Bug...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menu "
"bar of the application with the bug. This will open a small dialog box with "
"a link to the bug tracking system. Please make sure to follow the "
"instructions of the bug reporting wizard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "I want to program for &kde;. What should I do first?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Everybody is encouraged to develop software for &kde;. What you should do "
"first depends strongly on your experience, &eg; whether you have already "
"learned C++ or have experience with the &Qt; toolkit and so on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To get into &kde; programming, you will need some basic tools: "
"<application>cmake</application>, and <application>gcc</application>. You "
"should look to <ulink url=\"http://techbase.kde.org/\">http://techbase.kde."
"org/</ulink> for more tips."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Another excellent resource for learning &kde; programming is the &Qt; online "
"tutorials. These are installed along with &Qt;. To view them, open <filename>"
"$<envar>QTDIR</envar>/doc/html/index.html</filename> in &konqueror; and "
"bookmark it. The tutorials can be found under \"Using Qt\". The source code "
"for each lesson can be found in the <filename class=\"directory\">"
"$<envar>QTDIR</envar>/tutorial</filename> directory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is, however, one thing that everybody interested in programming for "
"&kde; should do: <emphasis>subscribe to the developers mailing list</"
"emphasis>. To subscribe, you have to send an email to <ulink url=\"mailto:"
"kde-devel-request@kde.org\">kde-devel-request@kde.org</ulink> with the "
"subject <userinput>subscribe <replaceable>your_email_address</replaceable></"
"userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please read <link linkend=\"subscribe\">How to subscribe/unsubscribe to "
"these lists</link> carefully. Everything said there applies to the "
"development list as well."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I get access to &kde; <acronym>SVN</acronym>?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kde; project uses <acronym>SVN</acronym> to develop the core parts of "
"the software. Usually, when you have changed one of the parts (&eg; fixed a "
"bug), and you want to commit this change, the best way is to create a patch "
"against a current snapshot and send this patch to the developer/maintainer "
"of the respective program."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are doing this more or less regularly, there are instructions here on "
"how to get write access to the <acronym>SVN</acronym> repository: <ulink url="
"\"http://techbase.kde.org/Contribute/Get_a_SVN_Account\"> http://techbase."
"kde.org/Contribute/Get_a_SVN_Account</ulink>. But be aware that more users "
"will slow down <acronym>SVN</acronym> access for all developers, so we want "
"to keep the number of people with direct <acronym>SVN</acronym> access "
"reasonably small. But feel free to ask!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can I have read-only access to the <acronym>SVN</acronym> repository?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes. Instructions on how to get anonymous, read-only <acronym>SVN</acronym> "
"access are here: <ulink url=\"http://techbase.kde.org/Getting_Started/"
"Sources/Anonymous_SVN\"> http://techbase.kde.org/Getting_Started/Sources/"
"Anonymous_SVN</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid "Are there any <acronym>SVN</acronym> mirror sites for &kde;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"No, there are currently no anonymous <acronym>SVN</acronym> mirror sites for "
"&kde;. If you're interested in setting one up, please contact "
"<email>sysadmin@kde.org</email>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I go about translating &kde; programs into my native language?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: contrib.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Look at the <ulink url=\"http://l10n.kde.org\">The &kde; Translators' and "
"Documenters' Web Site</ulink> to see whether your program is already "
"translated (most are). Otherwise you will find information there on how to "
"do it yourself."
msgstr ""
